00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:03.990 align:start position:0%
monster hunter rise is the next addition  in the gargantuanly popular beast  hunting series  we brave hunters have always gotten a  little help from our animal pals and in  rise we get even more  a rideable dog friend called a palomut  who has mobility in the world and some  flexibility in fights  there are tons of endemic species to  gather and each can have a huge impact  on your hunt through buffs to you and  blights to your prey  one of these new life forms called the  wire bug massively changes the way you  move and fight in the game  here's a quick overview of the new  systems in monster hunter rise  the palomood is a new companion addition  to monster hunter ryze who you can  choose to have accompany you along with  your paliko  while your palace goes gadgets support  you on hunts with buffs and debuffs the  palomute is a direct attacker in fights  but they're also rideable allowing you  to get around the map quicker than  ever without consuming stamina you can  perform attacks while mounted and just  like the palico the palamute is fully  customizable  and can wear armor the wire bug is  native to the lands around kamura  village and produces a substance called  iron silk which connects to the wire bug  and helps you get around during a hunt  you start with two wire bugs but you can  find another for a maximum of three  as you gather and prepare on your way to  a fight wire bug movement while your  weapon is sheathed is called a wire dash  with wire dash you can launch yourself  into the air suspend yourself from your  wire bug climb mountains and even wall  run until your stamina runs out or you  use another wire dash  if you get clobbered to the ground by a  monster the wire fall ability will get  you back on your feet immediately and  can then be paired with a wire dash to  quickly reposition yourself  you can attack from above by launching  into the air and attacking down onto  your prey  once you pull out your weapon iron silk  becomes deadly every one of the 14  different weapons gets  new super moves called silk bind attacks  which depending on the weapon can buff  your stats evade attacks or cause  huge damage to your prey each one has a  different wire bug charge cost and can  be swapped out so you can adjust your  hunter to your exact play style  lastly for the wire bug you can restrain  a monster with your iron silk and ride  it into battle for a short time using  the wyvern riding ability  while wyvern riding you can execute  light and heavy attacks and launch your  monster forward to smash into a wall or  another monster to do massive damage  attacking and evading will fill the  gauge for mounted punisher the monster's  ultimate ability which can then be used  on other monsters  wyvern riding can be triggered by  dealing damage with aerial and silk bind  attacks  getting monsters to fight each other in  turf wars or the easiest way  through an endemic pal called a puppet  spider which will instantly make a  monster rideable creatures that directly  help you while you're fighting like the  puppet spider are called hunting helpers  you can hold up to five of these little  guys in your helper cage and bring them  into battle to release when their  effects help you the most  they include trap bugs antedobra brew  hair  s cure go whale nard stink minks and  four different types of beetles that can  be thrown at monsters to inflict them  with debuffs called blights  the thunder beetle causes thunder blight  which allows for more stun damage to  monsters  the snow beetle causes ice blight to  slow enemies the fire beetle's fire  blight causes damage over time and  flinch while the mud beetle's water  blight softens enemy armor  other endemic life includes spira birds  who give you health  stamina attack or defense buffs until  the end of your quest  temporary buffs from creatures like the  cloth fly butter flame  peeper sex cutter fly and vigor wasp and  various plants including the jewel lily  that hides a great wire bug  monster hunter ryze is out on nintendo  switch on march 26th  i'll see you in the new rampage mode  don't miss out
 

